  "summary": "Independently read the complete spoken body and terminal apparatus of Learning to Hear the King against the canonical study and research, then checked the relevant 1962 Missal images at printed pp. 697\u2013698, nos. 3939\u20133940 and 3945\u20133949, Augustine's Tractate on John 115.1\u20134 and Psalm 28.10\u201311, and Chrysostom's Homilies on Colossians II on 1:12\u201315 and III on creation, reconciliation and liturgical peace: the revised Secret paragraph correctly distinguishes the Father addressed from the sacrificial Son who gives unity and peace, while the origin/presence distinction and grace-enabled hearing supply a text-dependent turn that connects the readings and prayers to concrete conversion and hope. All nine sealed files match; the body is speakable verbatim, contains 1,280 words (10.24\u201311.64 minutes at 125\u2013110 words per minute), preserves the study's argument without unsupported attribution or invented experience, and passes this homily review with no findings; timing remains a written estimate, with no audible rehearsal, timed human delivery or final rendered-page acceptance claimed."
